        "@language": "en-us",
        "@value": "Kathleen Edwards - Confederation Centre of the Arts"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-us",
        "@value": "For decades, Kathleen Edwards has been a cornerstone of North American roots music. Since making her debut with 2002's Failer, the Ottawa native has spent the 21st century swirling together her own mix of alt-country, folk, and heartland rock and roll - a sound that has earned her more than a half-dozen Juno nominations and Top 40 success on both sides of the Canadian/American border."
      }
    ],
