    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "PEI Symphony Orchestra Presents: Edge"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "With the season closer on April 11, Edge asks us to look beyond, and strive for better. The concert will open with Mozart’s Overture from ‘The Magic Flute’ which explores humanity’s never-ending mission to understand the beyond. ‘Bondarsphere’ traces the extraordinary life of Canadian astronaut Dr. Roberta Bondar in this original and inventive work by one of Canada’s great young talents, Montreal composer Nicole Lizée. Lizée employs soundtrack, video, and live orchestra, inviting the audience to reflect on Our Story in terms of Bondar’s trailblazing accomplishments, inciting a new generation to embrace a sense of discovery, experimentation and awe in the face of the infinite. In ‘O Virtus Sapeintiae,’ the reimagined 900-year-old music of Hildegard von Bingen, a German polymath and the first composer of written works by a woman, frames the concert as one of endeavour and ponderance. And Kevin Lau sonically explores ‘The Infinite Reaches’, while Richard Strauss’ towering ‘Death and Transfiguration’ ends the season with transformation, not to sadness, but to the next chapter of Our Story. The partnership between the P.E.I. Symphony Orchestra and Confederation Centre of the Arts is made possible through the Lou MacEachern Community Partnership Program, which fosters meaningful collaboration across Prince Edward [&hellip;]"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/keywords": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Music, On Stage"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ]
  },
